{
  "summary": "The proposed fix of capturing `current = self.focused` before `items_pane.focus()` addresses the root cause but is unnecessarily conservative. The real question the previous rounds sidestepped is: why is `items_pane.focus()` called at all? In Textual's focus model, focusing a child widget (StageHeader/FeatureItem) already makes its parent container scrollable and active—there is no need to explicitly focus the container first. The `items_pane.focus()` call is cargo-cult code that serves no purpose and introducing a workaround to preserve state around it adds complexity to compensate for a call that should simply be deleted. Additionally, the existing unit tests are structurally incapable of catching this bug: they mock `self.focused` as a direct attribute assignment, completely bypassing Textual's focus machinery, so they would pass identically whether `items_pane.focus()` is present or not. The tests give false confidence—an integration test using Textual's `pilot` test framework (which runs a real app and simulates key presses) is the only way to verify this fix actually works end-to-end."
}
